# Walkthrough - Resend Email Integration

I have successfully implemented a professional email submission system for your "Diagnóstico Preliminar" form.

## Changes Made

### 1. Server Action Integration
- **File**: [app/actions/send-email.ts](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/actions/send-email.ts)
- **Logic**: This "Server Action" receives the raw form data, formats it into a clean HTML layout with sections for "Datos de Identificación," "Perfil Operativo," and "Estado Actual," and sends it using the Resend API.
- **Recipient**: Configured to send to `sipracsiprac@gmail.com`.

### 2. Enhanced Contact Form
- **Component**: [components/contact/ContactForm.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/contact/ContactForm.tsx)
- **Dynamic States**: 
    - **Loading**: The button now shows a "Procesando Diagnóstico..." animation while sending.
    - **Success**: Upon successful submission, a friendly "¡Diagnóstico Enviado!" screen replaces the form, confirming that a consultant will follow up.
    - **Error Handling**: Added a shake-animated alert box if something goes wrong (e.g., API key missing or network issues).

### 3. Setup Template
- **File**: [.env.example](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/.env.example)
- Created a template file to help you set up your API Key safely.

### 4. FAQ Redesign (Premium Accordion)
- **Component**: [components/faq/DetailedFAQ.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/faq/DetailedFAQ.tsx)
- **Design Upgrade**:
    - Replaced the grid layout with a sleek, single-column accordion.
    - Added **Liquid Glass** effect with borders that glow on hover.
    - **Micro-animations**: Icons rotate 12 degrees when hovered, and items lift slightly for a tactile feel.
    - **Direct Contact**: Integrated WhatsApp buttons inside each answer to reduce friction for customer inquiries.

### 5. Immersion Neumorphic Benefits Cards
- **Component**: [components/sections/Benefits.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Benefits.tsx)
- **Visual Design**:
    - **Immersion Effect**: Switched to **inset shadows**, making the cards appear deep-carved into the screen background.
    - **Static Interaction**: Elements remain structurally static on hover to reinforce the solid, "carved" feel.
    - **Color Micro-interactions**: Smooth transitions on icon and text colors provide clear interactive feedback.

### 6. Unified Neumorphism (Mission & Vision)
- **Component**: [components/about/MissionVision.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/about/MissionVision.tsx)
- **Global Consistency**: Applied the same **inset shadow** system to the Mission and Vision sections.
- **Sculpted Aesthetic**: The cards and icon containers share the section background, appearing to be crafted from a single surface.

### 7. Unified Neumorphism (Corporate Values)
- **Component**: [components/about/CorporateValues.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/about/CorporateValues.tsx)
- **Refined Style**: Unified the Corporate Values with the persistent immersion effect, ensuring a cohesive travel experience across the entire website.
- **Semantic Highlighting**: Maintained visual hierarchy through typography and icon colors without disrupting the structural neumorphic system.

### 8. Enhanced Neumorphic Contact Cards
- **Component**: [components/contact/ContactInfo.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/contact/ContactInfo.tsx)
- **Visual & UI Refinement**:
    - **Larger Typography**: Significantly increased font sizes for titles (`text-3xl`), phone/email items (`text-base`), and general details to ensure maximum readability.
    - **Icon Integration**: Added the `PhoneForwarded` Lucide icon to telephone numbers, providing a clearer visual cue for the action.
    - **Balanced Layout**: Adjusted padding and spacing to accommodate larger text while maintaining the elegant immersion neumorphic effect.
    - **Direct Interaction**: Maintained high-contrast hover effects for color feedback.

### 9. Optimized Neumorphic FAQ Accordion
- **Components**: [components/contact/FAQ.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/contact/FAQ.tsx), [components/faq/DetailedFAQ.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/faq/DetailedFAQ.tsx)
- **Performance & Design**:
    - **Lag Elimination**: Removed heavy `liquid-glass` effects and hover translations to ensure zero-lag interactions.
    - **Immersion Unified**: Applied the persistent **inset shadow** system, making FAQ items appear deep-carved into the surface.
    - **Visual Consistency**: Unified the typography and spacing between the contact page FAQ and the detailed FAQ page.
    - **Tactile Details**: Inset shadows for icons and buttons within the accordion for a fully integrated look.

### 10. Animated Trayectoria Counters
- **Component**: [components/sections/Hero.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Hero.tsx)
- **Animation**: Implemented a state-of-the-art counter using `requestAnimationFrame` and an `easeOutQuad` function for a premium, fast-paced feel. The numbers count from 0 to their target values (100+, 50+, 15+) in 1.5 seconds.

### 11. Homepage Cleanup
- **Change**: Removed the "Misión" and "Visión" sections from the landing page ([app/page.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/page.tsx)) to streamline the user journey. These sections remain available on the "About" page.

### 12. Compact Neumorphic CTA Strategy
- **Component**: [components/sections/CTA.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/CTA.tsx)
- **Design**: Transformed the bulky Call-to-Action card into a sleek, horizontal strip that sits elegantly above the footer.
- **Style**: Applies the signature **immersion neumorphism** (inset shadows) to create a "carved path" effect, integrating the CTA seamlessly into the page flow rather than interrupting it.
- **Efficiency**: Reduced vertical footprint while maintaining high visibility through strategic spacing and high-contrast button placement.

### 13. Neumorphic Service Cards
- **Components**: [components/services/CoreAdvisory.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/CoreAdvisory.tsx), [components/services/ValuedAudits.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/ValuedAudits.tsx)
- **Design**: Extended the immersion neumorphism (inset shadows) to the main service cards.
- **Interactions**:
    - **Core Advisory**: Preserved the "Excelencia Operativa" bar expansion animation while changing the card to a static, carved appearance.
    - **Valued Audits**: Updated to a clean, inset look with consistent iconography, removing the "lifting" effect to prioritize the "carved" aesthetic.

### 14. Service Images Integration
- **Component**: [components/services/DetailedServices.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/DetailedServices.tsx)
- **Visuals**: Generated and integrated high-quality, professional images for each of the 6 service categories.
    - Used AI generation to create specific visuals for SST, Environmental Management, Quality, and Audits.
    - Ensured consistent lighting (warm/orange accents) and style (corporate, clean) to match the brand.
- **Assets**: Stored in `public/images/services/` for optimal loading.

### 15. Favicon Configuration
- **Issue**: Standard [favicon.ico](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/favicon.ico) was blocked by conflicting manual overrides in [layout.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/layout.tsx).
- **Fix**: Removed redundant `<link>` tags and metadata overrides. Next.js now automatically renders the favicon located in the app root using standard best practices.

### 16. Email Template Styling
- **Component**: [app/actions/send-email.ts](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/actions/send-email.ts)
- **Design**: Created a responsive HTML email template simulating the site's branding.
    - **Palette**: `#FAF9F6` background, Clean White Data Cards, Orange `#f97316` Accents.
    - **Structure**: Rounded "glass-like" cards with subtle borders (email-safe neumorphism).
    - **Footer**: Dark branded footer for professional finish.

### 17. UI Enhancements (Mobile Nav & Services)
- **Mobile Navbar**: 
    - Implemented a slide-in sidebar menu from the left.
    - Added a **Backdrop Blur Focus Effect**: When the menu opens, the page background blurs heavily (`backdrop-blur-[8px]`), effectively focusing the user's attention on the navigation.
- **Home Services**:
    - Redesigned with a **Geometric Neumorphic Style**.
    - **Reusable Card Component**: Created [NeumorphicCard](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Services.tsx#68-106).
    - **Shadows**: Specific request applied: Light Shadow Top-Left (`-10px -10px`), Dark Shadow Bottom-Right (`10px 10px`) effectively creating a raised, extruded block look.

### 18. UX Optimizations (Mobile & Animations)
- **Mobile Carousels**:
    - Converted long vertical stacks in [CoreAdvisory](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/CoreAdvisory.tsx#39-104), [ValuedAudits](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/ValuedAudits.tsx#33-79), and [DetailedServices](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/DetailedServices.tsx#100-181) into **horizontal swipeable carousels** on mobile devices.
    - Used CSS Snap logic (`snap-x`, `snap-center`) for a native app-like feel.
    - Drastically reduced page length on mobile while keeping content accessible.
- **Scroll-Triggered Animations**:
    - Updated [AnimatedCounter](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Hero.tsx#5-66) in the Hero section.
    - Now uses `IntersectionObserver` to trigger the counting animation **only when the user scrolls the numbers into view**, ensuring the effect isn't missed.

### 19. Final Mobile Polish
- **Benefits Section**: Converted to a swipeable carousel on mobile ([Benefits.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Benefits.tsx)).
- **Mobile Header**: 
    - Exposed the **Request Advisory** button on the mobile navbar.
    - Updated layout to `[Toggle] [Logo] [Button]` for optimal reachability and immediate access to the primary CTA.
    - Simplified button text to "Asesoría" on small screens to save space.

### 20. Detailed Services Cards
- **Issue**: "DetailedServices" items were too loose on mobile, causing reading flow issues.
- **Fix**: Wrapped each service detail in a **unified Card container** on mobile.
    - **Mobile Layout**: Image Top + Content Bottom, all enclosed in a white rounded card with shadow.
    - **Desktop Layout**: Preserved the original Zig-Zag alternating layout (No card enclosure).
    - Result: A clean card-based carousel on mobile that matches the app-like feel of the other sections.

### 21. Mobile UX: Full-Screen Text Cards
- **Refinement**: User requested cards to be "screen size" to ensure absolutely no information is cut off.
- **Implementation**:
    - **Full Width**: Updated card width to `min-w-full`. This forces one card per view, maximizing horizontal space for text.
    - **Text-Only & Neumorphic**: Maintained the image-less, tactile card design on mobile for clarity.
    - **Result**: optimal readability without horizontal constraints or cut-off text.

### 22. Standardized Mobile Carousels
- **Consistency Update**: Applied the same "manual swipe" carousel interaction pattern from the Benefits section to the **Advisory** and **Services** sections.
- **Changes**:
    - **CoreAdvisory ([CoreAdvisory.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/CoreAdvisory.tsx))**: Updated mobile container to use consistent padding (`-mx-4 px-4`) and snap logic.
    - **Services ([Services.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Services.tsx))**: 
        -   **Desktop**: Retained the "Infinite Scroll" animation.
        -   **Mobile**: Disabled auto-scroll and replaced it with a manual swipeable carousel. This gives mobile users better control and interactions consistent with the rest of the site.
        -   Hidden edge gradients on mobile to avoid obscuring the swipe area.

